IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-theft.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "Theft": sections 322 to 334.1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- READING A RESULT (details in NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)"): JUST TRUE = the facts bring the case within the provision;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (the comment names the words); NOTHING = the text does not answer (the comment says why).
-- A function is named for the positive proposition a person asks ("commits theft"). Where the text states a flat negative with its own limit
-- ("does not commit theft by pledging ... if ..."), the case inside the limit is JUST FALSE and the case outside it is NOTHING.
-- Answers taken from another provision are INPUTS named for that provision (`s 2 <term>: ...`, `s 322 ...`, `s 787(1) ...`), typed as the answering
-- provision answers (MAYBE BOOLEAN where it can answer NOTHING); a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Theft (ss 322 to 334.1)`

§§ `Section 322 -- theft`

-- "Every one commits theft who ..." is read as the provision's own question: an element that fails is JUST FALSE (fork F-OFFENCE in NOTES.md).
-- src:6534 | Theft
-- src:6535 | 322 (1) Every one commits theft who fraudulently and without colour of right takes, or fraudulently and without colour of right converts to his use or to the use of another person, anything, whether animate or inanimate, with intent
-- src:6536 | (a) to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of his property or interest in it;
-- src:6537 | (b) to pledge it or deposit it as security;
-- src:6538 | (c) to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that the person who parts with it may be unable to perform; or
-- src:6539 | (d) to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was at the time it was taken or converted.
@ref Criminal Code s 322(1) (src:6534-6539)
GIVEN `the person fraudulently and without colour of right took anything, whether animate or inanimate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently and without colour of right converted anything, whether animate or inanimate, to their use or to the use of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent was to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of their property or interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent was to pledge it or deposit it as security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent was to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that the person who parts with it may be unable to perform` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent was to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was at the time it was taken or converted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322(1) the person commits theft` MEANS
    IF    (   `the person fraudulently and without colour of right took anything, whether animate or inanimate`
           OR `the person fraudulently and without colour of right converted anything, whether animate or inanimate, to their use or to the use of another person`)
      AND (   `the intent was to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of their property or interest in it`
           OR `the intent was to pledge it or deposit it as security`
           OR `the intent was to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that the person who parts with it may be unable to perform`
           OR `the intent was to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was at the time it was taken or converted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits theft who fraudulently and without colour of right takes, or fraudulently and without colour of right converts"

-- src:6540 | Time when theft completed
-- src:6541 | (2) A person commits theft when, with intent to steal anything, he moves it or causes it to move or to be moved, or begins to cause it to become movable.
@ref Criminal Code s 322(2) (src:6540-6541)
GIVEN `the person has intent to steal anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person moves it or causes it to move or to be moved, or begins to cause it to become movable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322(2) the person commits theft by moving the thing` MEANS
    IF `the person has intent to steal anything` AND `the person moves it or causes it to move or to be moved, or begins to cause it to become movable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits theft when, with intent to steal anything, he moves it" ("when" counts as "where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), (c); fork F-WHEN)

-- The seam asked by the keel's `s 2 steal` (PLAN.md section 6): `s 322 the person commits theft`: MAYBE BOOLEAN. Subsection (2) is read as a second route to theft (fork F-322-2).
-- src:6535 | 322 (1) Every one commits theft who fraudulently and without colour of right takes, or fraudulently and without colour of right converts to his use or to the use of another person, anything, whether animate or inanimate, with intent
-- src:6536 | (a) to deprive, temporarily or absolutely, the owner of it, or a person who has a special property or interest in it, of the thing or of his property or interest in it;
-- src:6537 | (b) to pledge it or deposit it as security;
-- src:6538 | (c) to part with it under a condition with respect to its return that the person who parts with it may be unable to perform; or
-- src:6539 | (d) to deal with it in such a manner that it cannot be restored in the condition in which it was at the time it was taken or converted.
-- src:6540 | Time when theft completed
-- src:6541 | (2) A person commits theft when, with intent to steal anything, he moves it or causes it to move or to be moved, or begins to cause it to become movable.
@ref Criminal Code s 322 (src:6535-6541)
GIVEN `the person commits theft, by s 322(1) the person commits theft` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits theft by moving the thing, by s 322(2) the person commits theft by moving the thing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322 the person commits theft` MEANS
    `ccc12 or` `the person commits theft, by s 322(1) the person commits theft` `the person commits theft by moving the thing, by s 322(2) the person commits theft by moving the thing`
    -- JUST FALSE only when both routes are definite no's: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits theft who" (subsection (1)) and "A person commits theft when" (subsection (2))

-- src:6542 | Secrecy
-- src:6543 | (3) A taking or conversion of anything may be fraudulent notwithstanding that it is effected without secrecy or attempt at concealment.
@ref Criminal Code s 322(3) (src:6542-6543)
GIVEN `the taking or conversion was effected without secrecy or attempt at concealment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322(3) the absence of secrecy prevents the taking or conversion from being fraudulent` MEANS
    IF `the taking or conversion was effected without secrecy or attempt at concealment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be fraudulent notwithstanding that it is effected without secrecy or attempt at concealment"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) says nothing where there was secrecy

DECLARE `s 322(4) question` IS ONE OF
    `s 322(4) whether anything that is converted is taken for the purpose of conversion`
    `s 322(4) whether it is, at the time it is converted, in the lawful possession of the person who converts it`
    `s 322(4) another question`

-- src:6544 | Purpose of taking
-- src:6545 | (4) For the purposes of this Act, the question whether anything that is converted is taken for the purpose of conversion, or whether it is, at the time it is converted, in the lawful possession of the person who converts it is not material.
@ref Criminal Code s 322(4) (src:6544-6545)
GIVEN question IS A `s 322(4) question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322(4) the question is material` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 322(4) whether anything that is converted is taken for the purpose of conversion` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not material"
    WHEN `s 322(4) whether it is, at the time it is converted, in the lawful possession of the person who converts it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not material"
    WHEN `s 322(4) another question` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (4) names only the two questions

-- src:6546 | Wild living creature
-- src:6547 | (5) For the purposes of this section, a person who has a wild living creature in captivity shall be deemed to have a special property or interest in it while it is in captivity and after it has escaped from captivity.
@ref Criminal Code s 322(5) (src:6546-6547)
GIVEN `the person has a wild living creature in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creature is in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creature has escaped from captivity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 322(5) the person is deemed to have a special property or interest in the creature` MEANS
    IF `the person has a wild living creature in captivity` AND (`the creature is in captivity` OR `the creature has escaped from captivity`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person who has a wild living creature in captivity shall be deemed to have a special property or interest in it while it is in captivity and after it has escaped from captivity" (a deeming provision's own question: fork F-DEEM)

§§ `Section 323 -- oysters`

-- src:6548 | Oysters
-- src:6549 | 323 (1) Where oysters and oyster brood are in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of any person and are sufficiently marked out or known as the property of that person, that person shall be deemed to have a special property or interest in them.
@ref Criminal Code s 323(1) (src:6548-6549)
GIVEN `oysters and oyster brood are in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the oyster beds, layings or fisheries are sufficiently marked out or known as the property of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 323(1) the person is deemed to have a special property or interest in the oysters and oyster brood` MEANS
    IF `oysters and oyster brood are in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of any person` AND `the oyster beds, layings or fisheries are sufficiently marked out or known as the property of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where oysters and oyster brood are in oyster beds, layings or fisheries that are the property of any person and are sufficiently marked out or known as the property of that person" ("Where" gate failing: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F-DEEM)

-- "An indictment is sufficient if it describes an oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way, without stating that it is situated in a particular territorial division."
-- The absence of a statement of the territorial division makes no difference, so no input asks for it.
-- src:6550 | Oyster bed
-- src:6551 | (2) An indictment is sufficient if it describes an oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way, without stating that it is situated in a particular territorial division.
@ref Criminal Code s 323(2) (src:6550-6551)
GIVEN `the indictment describes an oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 323(2) the indictment is sufficient` MEANS
    IF `the indictment describes an oyster bed, laying or fishery by name or in any other way`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says when an indictment is sufficient, not when it is insufficient

§§ `Section 324 -- theft by a bailee of things under seizure`

-- src:6552 | Theft by bailee of things under seizure
-- src:6553 | 324 Every one who is a bailee of anything that is under lawful seizure by a peace officer or public officer in the execution of the duties of his office, and who is obliged by law or agreement to produce and deliver it to that officer or to another person entitled thereto at a certain time and place, or on demand, steals it if he does not produce and deliver it in accordance with his obligation, but he does not steal it if his failure to produce and deliver it is not the result of a wilful act or omission by him.
@ref Criminal Code s 324 (src:6552-6553)
GIVEN `the person is a bailee of anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is under lawful seizure in the execution of the duties of the office of the seizing officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seizing officer is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the seizing officer is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is obliged by law or agreement to produce and deliver it to that officer or to another person entitled thereto at a certain time and place, or on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did not produce and deliver it in accordance with the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to produce and deliver it is the result of a wilful act or omission by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 324 the bailee steals the thing under seizure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the failure to produce and deliver it is the result of a wilful act or omission by the person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but he does not steal it if his failure to produce and deliver it is not the result of a wilful act or omission by him"
        IF    `the person is a bailee of anything`
          AND `the thing is under lawful seizure in the execution of the duties of the office of the seizing officer`
          AND `the person is obliged by law or agreement to produce and deliver it to that officer or to another person entitled thereto at a certain time and place, or on demand`
          AND `the person did not produce and deliver it in accordance with the obligation`
        THEN `ccc12 or` `the seizing officer is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` `the seizing officer is a public officer, by s 2 public officer`
             -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answers of s 2 "peace officer" and s 2 "public officer" were not given
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "steals it if he does not produce and deliver it in accordance with his obligation"

§§ `Section 325 -- agent pledging goods, when not theft`

-- src:6554 | Agent pledging goods, when not theft
-- src:6555 | 325 A factor or an agent does not commit theft by pledging or giving a lien on goods or documents of title to goods that are entrusted to him for the purpose of sale or for any other purpose, if the pledge or lien is for an amount that does not exceed the sum of
-- src:6556 | (a) the amount due to him from his principal at the time the goods or documents are pledged or the lien is given; and
-- src:6557 | (b) the amount of any bill of exchange that he has accepted for or on account of his principal.
@ref Criminal Code s 325 (src:6554-6557)
GIVEN `the person is a factor or an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods or documents of title to goods are entrusted to the person for the purpose of sale or for any other purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person pledges them or gives a lien on them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount for which the pledge or lien is given, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount due to the person from the principal at the time the goods or documents are pledged or the lien is given, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of any bill of exchange that the person has accepted for or on account of the principal, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 325 the factor or agent commits theft by pledging or giving a lien on goods or documents of title to goods` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a factor or an agent`
      AND `the goods or documents of title to goods are entrusted to the person for the purpose of sale or for any other purpose`
      AND `the person pledges them or gives a lien on them`
      AND `the amount for which the pledge or lien is given, in dollars` AT MOST (`the amount due to the person from the principal at the time the goods or documents are pledged or the lien is given, in dollars` PLUS `the amount of any bill of exchange that the person has accepted for or on account of the principal, in dollars`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A factor or an agent does not commit theft by pledging or giving a lien on goods or documents of title to goods"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section says no only for a pledge or lien that does not exceed the sum of (a) and (b); it does not say that a larger pledge is theft

§§ `Section 326 -- theft of telecommunication service`

-- src:6558 | Theft of telecommunication service
-- src:6559 | 326 (1) Every one commits theft who fraudulently, maliciously, or without colour of right,
-- src:6560 | (a) abstracts, consumes or uses electricity or gas or causes it to be wasted or diverted; or
-- src:6561 | (b) uses any telecommunication facility or obtains any telecommunication service.
@ref Criminal Code s 326(1) (src:6558-6561)
GIVEN `the person acted fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted without colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person abstracts, consumes or uses electricity or gas or causes it to be wasted or diverted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses any telecommunication facility or obtains any telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 326(1) the person commits theft of electricity, gas or a telecommunication service` MEANS
    IF    (`the person acted fraudulently` OR `the person acted maliciously` OR `the person acted without colour of right`)
      AND (`the person abstracts, consumes or uses electricity or gas or causes it to be wasted or diverted` OR `the person uses any telecommunication facility or obtains any telecommunication service`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits theft who fraudulently, maliciously, or without colour of right"

-- src:6562 | (2) [Repealed, 2014, c. 31, s. 14]
@ref Criminal Code s 326(2) (src:6562)
`s 326(2) as the text shows it` MEANS "(2) [Repealed, 2014, c. 31, s. 14]"

§§ `Section 327 -- possession of a device to obtain the use of a telecommunication facility or service`

-- src:6563 | Possession of device to obtain use of telecommunication facility or service
-- src:6564 | 327 (1) Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available a device that is designed or adapted primarily to use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service without payment of a lawful charge, knowing that the device has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose, is
-- src:6565 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:6566 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 327(1) (src:6563-6566)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a device, by s 327(4) the thing is a device` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the device is designed or adapted primarily to use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service without payment of a lawful charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the device has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(1) the person commits the offence of possessing a device to obtain the use of a telecommunication facility or service` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `the person makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available the thing`
      AND `the device is designed or adapted primarily to use a telecommunication facility or obtain a telecommunication service without payment of a lawful charge`
      AND `the person knows that the device has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose`
    THEN `the thing is a device, by s 327(4) the thing is a device`   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the answer of subsection (4), "device includes", was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, makes, possesses, sells, offers for sale, imports, obtains for use, distributes or makes available a device"

-- Subsection (1)(a) and (b): the summary limb states no penalty, so the general penalty of s 787(1) is an input.
@ref Criminal Code s 327(1) (src:6564-6566)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 327(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than two years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6567 | Forfeiture
-- src:6568 | (2) If a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1) or paragraph 326(1)(b), in addition to any punishment that is imposed, any device in relation to which the offence was committed or the possession of which constituted the offence may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty and may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 327(2) (src:6567-6568)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 327(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted of an offence under paragraph 326(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device is one in relation to which the offence was committed, or the possession of which constituted the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(2) the device may be ordered forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF    (`the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 327(1)` OR `the person is convicted of an offence under paragraph 326(1)(b)`)
      AND `the device is one in relation to which the offence was committed, or the possession of which constituted the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may be ordered forfeited") named for a conviction under (1) or paragraph 326(1)(b) and a device connected with the offence; outside that limit the subsection grants nothing and denies nothing

GIVEN `the device has been ordered forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 327(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(2) the device may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs` MEANS
    IF `the device has been ordered forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 327(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the direction is of a device ordered forfeited

-- src:6569 | Limitation
-- src:6570 | (3) No order for forfeiture is to be made in respect of telecommunication facilities or equipment by means of which an offence under subsection (1) is committed if they are owned by a person engaged in providing a telecommunication service to the public or form part of such a person’s telecommunication service or system and that person is not a party to the offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 327(3) (src:6569-6570)
GIVEN `the thing is telecommunication facilities or equipment by means of which an offence under subsection 327(1) is committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are owned by a person engaged in providing a telecommunication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they form part of the telecommunication service or system of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is not a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(3) an order for forfeiture is barred` MEANS
    IF    `the thing is telecommunication facilities or equipment by means of which an offence under subsection 327(1) is committed`
      AND (`they are owned by a person engaged in providing a telecommunication service to the public` OR `they form part of the telecommunication service or system of such a person`)
      AND `that person is not a party to the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No order for forfeiture is to be made in respect of telecommunication facilities or equipment by means of which an offence under subsection (1) is committed if" (a failed "if" gate: reading (a) of the Marginal readings)

-- "device includes (a) a component of a device; and (b) a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2)." An "includes" definition: the list is open.
-- src:6571 | Definition of device
-- src:6572 | (4) In this section, device includes
-- src:6573 | (a) a component of a device; and
-- src:6574 | (b) a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 327(4) (src:6571-6574)
GIVEN `it is a component of a device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 327(4) the thing is a device` MEANS
    IF `it is a component of a device`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "device includes" lists without closing the list
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of subsection 342.1(2) was not given

§§ `Section 328 -- theft by or from a person having a special property or interest`

DECLARE `s 328 circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 328 stolen by the owner of it from a person who has a special property or interest in it`
    `s 328 stolen by a person who has a special property or interest in it from the owner of it`
    `s 328 stolen by a lessee of it from his reversioner`
    `s 328 stolen by one of several joint owners, tenants in common or partners of or in it from the other persons who have an interest in it`
    `s 328 stolen by the representatives of an organization from the organization`
    `s 328 stolen in another circumstance`

-- src:6575 | Theft by or from person having special property or interest
-- src:6576 | 328 A person may be convicted of theft notwithstanding that anything that is alleged to have been stolen was stolen
-- src:6577 | (a) by the owner of it from a person who has a special property or interest in it;
-- src:6578 | (b) by a person who has a special property or interest in it from the owner of it;
-- src:6579 | (c) by a lessee of it from his reversioner;
-- src:6580 | (d) by one of several joint owners, tenants in common or partners of or in it from the other persons who have an interest in it; or
-- src:6581 | (e) by the representatives of an organization from the organization.
@ref Criminal Code s 328 (src:6575-6581)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 328 circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 328 the person may be convicted of theft notwithstanding the circumstance` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 328 stolen by the owner of it from a person who has a special property or interest in it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 328 stolen by a person who has a special property or interest in it from the owner of it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 328 stolen by a lessee of it from his reversioner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 328 stolen by one of several joint owners, tenants in common or partners of or in it from the other persons who have an interest in it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 328 stolen by the representatives of an organization from the organization` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 328 stolen in another circumstance` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section names five circumstances and does not say that no other qualifies

-- src:6582 | 329 [Repealed, 2000, c. 12, s. 94]
@ref Criminal Code s 329 (src:6582)
`s 329 as the text shows it` MEANS "329 [Repealed, 2000, c. 12, s. 94]"

§§ `Sections 330 to 333 -- theft by a person required to account, by attorney, by misappropriation; ore specimens`

-- src:6583 | Theft by person required to account
-- src:6584 | 330 (1) Every one commits theft who, having received anything from any person on terms that require him to account for or pay it or the proceeds of it or a part of the proceeds to that person or another person, fraudulently fails to account for or pay it or the proceeds of it or the part of the proceeds of it accordingly.
@ref Criminal Code s 330(1) (src:6583-6584)
GIVEN `the person received anything from any person on terms that require them to account for or pay it or the proceeds of it or a part of the proceeds to that person or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently failed to account for or pay it or the proceeds of it or the part of the proceeds of it accordingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(1) the person commits theft by failing to account` MEANS
    IF    `the person received anything from any person on terms that require them to account for or pay it or the proceeds of it or a part of the proceeds to that person or another person`
      AND `the person fraudulently failed to account for or pay it or the proceeds of it or the part of the proceeds of it accordingly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits theft who, having received anything from any person on terms that require him to account for or pay it"

-- src:6585 | Effect of entry in account
-- src:6586 | (2) Where subsection (1) otherwise applies, but one of the terms is that the thing received or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it shall be an item in a debtor and creditor account between the person who receives the thing and the person to whom he is to account for or to pay it, and that the latter shall rely only on the liability of the other as his debtor in respect thereof, a proper entry in that account of the thing received or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it, as the case may be, is a sufficient accounting therefor, and no fraudulent conversion of the thing or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it thereby accounted for shall be deemed to have taken place.
@ref Criminal Code s 330(2) (src:6585-6586)
GIVEN `subsection 330(1) otherwise applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the terms is that the thing received or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it shall be an item in a debtor and creditor account between the person who receives the thing and the person to whom they are to account for or to pay it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the terms is that the latter shall rely only on the liability of the other as their debtor in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proper entry in that account of the thing received or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 330(2) a fraudulent conversion of the thing or the proceeds is deemed to have taken place` MEANS
    IF    `subsection 330(1) otherwise applies`
      AND `one of the terms is that the thing received or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it shall be an item in a debtor and creditor account between the person who receives the thing and the person to whom they are to account for or to pay it`
      AND `one of the terms is that the latter shall rely only on the liability of the other as their debtor in respect of it`
      AND `a proper entry in that account of the thing received or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it has been made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no fraudulent conversion of the thing or the proceeds or part of the proceeds of it thereby accounted for shall be deemed to have taken place"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks only where (1) otherwise applies, the two terms are present and a proper entry has been made

-- src:6587 | Theft by person holding power of attorney
-- src:6588 | 331 Every one commits theft who, being entrusted, whether solely or jointly with another person, with a power of attorney for the sale, mortgage, pledge or other disposition of real or personal property, fraudulently sells, mortgages, pledges or otherwise disposes of the property or any part of it, or fraudulently converts the proceeds of a sale, mortgage, pledge or other disposition of the property, or any part of the proceeds, to a purpose other than that for which he was entrusted by the power of attorney.
@ref Criminal Code s 331 (src:6587-6588)
GIVEN `the person was entrusted, whether solely or jointly with another person, with a power of attorney for the sale, mortgage, pledge or other disposition of real or personal property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently sells, mortgages, pledges or otherwise disposes of the property or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently converts the proceeds of a sale, mortgage, pledge or other disposition of the property, or any part of the proceeds, to a purpose other than that for which they were entrusted by the power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 331 the person commits theft by disposing of property held under a power of attorney` MEANS
    IF    `the person was entrusted, whether solely or jointly with another person, with a power of attorney for the sale, mortgage, pledge or other disposition of real or personal property`
      AND (   `the person fraudulently sells, mortgages, pledges or otherwise disposes of the property or any part of it`
           OR `the person fraudulently converts the proceeds of a sale, mortgage, pledge or other disposition of the property, or any part of the proceeds, to a purpose other than that for which they were entrusted by the power of attorney`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits theft who, being entrusted, whether solely or jointly with another person, with a power of attorney"

-- src:6589 | Misappropriation of money held under direction
-- src:6590 | 332 (1) Every one commits theft who, having received, either solely or jointly with another person, money or valuable security or a power of attorney for the sale of real or personal property, with a direction that the money or a part of it, or the proceeds or a part of the proceeds of the security or the property shall be applied to a purpose or paid to a person specified in the direction, fraudulently and contrary to the direction applies to any other purpose or pays to any other person the money or proceeds or any part of it.
@ref Criminal Code s 332(1) (src:6589-6590)
GIVEN `the person received, either solely or jointly with another person, money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person received, either solely or jointly with another person, a valuable security, by s 2 valuable security` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person received, either solely or jointly with another person, a power of attorney for the sale of real or personal property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person received it with a direction that the money or a part of it, or the proceeds or a part of the proceeds of the security or the property, shall be applied to a purpose or paid to a person specified in the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently and contrary to the direction applied the money or proceeds or any part of it to any other purpose or paid it to any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 332(1) the person commits theft by misappropriating money held under direction` MEANS
    IF    `the person received it with a direction that the money or a part of it, or the proceeds or a part of the proceeds of the security or the property, shall be applied to a purpose or paid to a person specified in the direction`
      AND `the person fraudulently and contrary to the direction applied the money or proceeds or any part of it to any other purpose or paid it to any other person`
    THEN `ccc12 or` (JUST (`the person received, either solely or jointly with another person, money` OR `the person received, either solely or jointly with another person, a power of attorney for the sale of real or personal property`))
                    `the person received, either solely or jointly with another person, a valuable security, by s 2 valuable security`
         -- JUST FALSE when money, power of attorney and valuable security are all definite no's: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "having received, either solely or jointly with another person, money or valuable security or a power of attorney for the sale of real or personal property"
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 2 "valuable security" was not given and money and power of attorney are not received
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with a direction that the money or a part of it, or the proceeds or a part of the proceeds of the security or the property shall be applied to a purpose or paid to a person specified in the direction, fraudulently and contrary to the direction"

-- (2): "This section does not apply where [the two deal on debtor-and-creditor terms], unless the direction is in writing." The "unless" once met: NOTHING (fork F-UNLESS).
-- src:6591 | Effect of entry in account
-- src:6592 | (2) This section does not apply where a person who receives anything mentioned in subsection (1) and the person from whom he receives it deal with each other on such terms that all money paid to the former would, in the absence of any such direction, be properly treated as an item in a debtor and creditor account between them, unless the direction is in writing.
@ref Criminal Code s 332(2) (src:6591-6592)
GIVEN `the person who receives anything mentioned in subsection (1) and the person from whom they receive it deal with each other on such terms that all money paid to the former would, in the absence of any such direction, be properly treated as an item in a debtor and creditor account between them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 332(2) section 332 applies to the receipt` MEANS
    IF    `the person who receives anything mentioned in subsection (1) and the person from whom they receive it deal with each other on such terms that all money paid to the former would, in the absence of any such direction, be properly treated as an item in a debtor and creditor account between them`
      AND NOT `the direction is in writing`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply where a person who receives anything mentioned in subsection (1) and the person from whom he receives it deal with each other on such terms that all money paid to the former would, in the absence of any such direction, be properly treated as an item in a debtor and creditor account between them, unless the direction is in writing"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says no only for debtor-and-creditor terms with a direction not in writing; where the direction is in writing ("unless" met), or the terms differ, it says nothing about whether the section applies

-- src:6593 | Taking ore for scientific purpose
-- src:6594 | 333 No person commits theft by reason only that he takes, for the purpose of exploration or scientific investigation, a specimen of ore or mineral from land that is not enclosed and is not occupied or worked as a mine, quarry or digging.
@ref Criminal Code s 333 (src:6593-6594)
GIVEN `the person takes a specimen of ore or mineral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of taking it is exploration or scientific investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land is not enclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land is not occupied or worked as a mine, quarry or digging` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333 the person commits theft by reason only of taking a specimen of ore or mineral for exploration or scientific investigation` MEANS
    IF    `the person takes a specimen of ore or mineral`
      AND `the purpose of taking it is exploration or scientific investigation`
      AND `the land is not enclosed`
      AND `the land is not occupied or worked as a mine, quarry or digging`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits theft by reason only that he takes, for the purpose of exploration or scientific investigation, a specimen of ore or mineral from land that is not enclosed and is not occupied or worked as a mine, quarry or digging"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only" and the land and purpose conditions limit the no; outside them section 333 says nothing

§§ `Sections 333.1 to 333.2 -- motor vehicle theft`

-- src:6595 | Motor vehicle theft
-- src:6596 | 333.1 (1) Everyone who commits theft is, if the property stolen is a motor vehicle, guilty of an offence and liable
-- src:6597 | (a) on proceedings by way of indictment, to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months in the case of a third or subsequent offence under this subsection; or
-- src:6598 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.1(1) (src:6595-6598)
GIVEN `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property stolen is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.1(1) the person is guilty of the offence of motor vehicle theft` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` `the property stolen is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle`
    -- JUST FALSE where either is a definite no: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone who commits theft is, if the property stolen is a motor vehicle, guilty of an offence"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 322 answer or the s 2 "motor vehicle" answer was not given

-- (2): an offence for which the person was previously convicted counts as an earlier offence whether it was prosecuted by indictment or by summary conviction.
-- src:6599 | Subsequent offences
-- src:6600 | (2) For the purpose of determining whether a convicted person has committed a third or subsequent offence, an offence for which the person was previously convicted is considered to be an earlier offence whether it was prosecuted by indictment or by way of summary conviction proceedings.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.1(2) (src:6599-6600)
GIVEN `the person was previously convicted of an offence under subsection 333.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mode in which the earlier offence was prosecuted` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.1(2) the earlier conviction is considered to be an earlier offence` MEANS
    IF `the person was previously convicted of an offence under subsection 333.1(1)`
    THEN CONSIDER `the mode in which the earlier offence was prosecuted`
         WHEN `by indictment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence for which the person was previously convicted is considered to be an earlier offence"

-- The punishment limbs of (1): (a) on indictment, not more than 10 years and a minimum of six months for a third or subsequent offence; (b) on summary conviction, not more than two years less a day.
-- src:6596 | 333.1 (1) Everyone who commits theft is, if the property stolen is a motor vehicle, guilty of an offence and liable
-- src:6597 | (a) on proceedings by way of indictment, to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months in the case of a third or subsequent offence under this subsection; or
-- src:6598 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.1(1) (src:6596-6598)
GIVEN `the number of earlier offences counted under subsection 333.1(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 333.1(1) the punishment for motor vehicle theft` MEANS
    LIST IF `the number of earlier offences counted under subsection 333.1(2)` AT LEAST 2
         THEN `ccc12 an indictable limb with a minimum` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) (`imprisonment for a term of` `six months`)   -- (a) a third or subsequent offence: minimum six months
         ELSE `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) a first or second offence: no minimum stated
       , `ccc12 a summary limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`)   -- (b)

-- src:6601 | Motor vehicle theft when violence used, threatened or attempted
-- src:6602 | (3) Everyone who commits theft in the commission of which violence against a person is used, threatened or attempted is, if the property stolen is a motor vehicle, guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.1(3) (src:6601-6602)
GIVEN `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `violence against a person is used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the theft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property stolen is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.1(3) the person is guilty of the offence of motor vehicle theft with violence` MEANS
    IF `violence against a person is used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the theft`
    THEN `ccc12 and` `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` `the property stolen is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle`
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 322 answer or the s 2 "motor vehicle" answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone who commits theft in the commission of which violence against a person is used, threatened or attempted"

@ref Criminal Code s 333.1(3) (src:6602-6602)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 333.1(3) the punishment for motor vehicle theft with violence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:6603 | Motor vehicle theft for criminal organization
-- src:6604 | (4) Everyone who commits theft for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization is, if the property stolen is a motor vehicle, guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.1(4) (src:6603-6604)
GIVEN `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the theft is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the property stolen is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.1(4) the person is guilty of the offence of motor vehicle theft for a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the theft is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization`
    THEN `ccc12 and` (`ccc12 and` `the person commits theft, by s 322 the person commits theft` `the property stolen is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle`) `the group is a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization`
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 322, s 2 "motor vehicle" or s 2 "criminal organization" answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone who commits theft for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization"

@ref Criminal Code s 333.1(4) (src:6604-6604)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 333.1(4) the punishment for motor vehicle theft for a criminal organization` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:6605 | Sentences to be served consecutively — breaking and entering
-- src:6606 | 333.11 (1) A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4) shall be served consecutively to any other sentence imposed on the person for an offence under section 348 arising out of the same event or series of events.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.11(1) (src:6605-6606)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under section 348` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence under section 348 arises out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.11(1) the sentence shall be served consecutively to the other sentence` MEANS
    IF    `the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4)`
      AND `the other sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under section 348`
      AND `the offence under section 348 arises out of the same event or series of events`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4) shall be served consecutively to any other sentence imposed on the person for an offence under section 348 arising out of the same event or series of events" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)

-- src:6607 | Sentences to be served consecutively — other offences
-- src:6608 | (2) A sentence imposed on a person for a second or subsequent offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4) shall be served consecutively to any other sentence imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.11(2) (src:6607-6608)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed on the person for a second or subsequent offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other sentence is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.11(2) the sentence shall be served consecutively to the other sentence` MEANS
    IF    `the sentence is imposed on the person for a second or subsequent offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4)`
      AND `the other sentence is imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sentence imposed on a person for a second or subsequent offence under subsection 333.1(3) or (4) shall be served consecutively to any other sentence imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)

-- src:6609 | Possession of device for purpose of committing theft
-- src:6610 | 333.2 (1) Everyone commits an offence who possesses an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle for the purpose of committing a motor vehicle theft offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.2(1) (src:6609-6610)
GIVEN `the person possesses an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it for the purpose of committing a motor vehicle theft offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.2(1) the person commits the offence of possessing an electronic device for the purpose of committing motor vehicle theft` MEANS
    IF    `the person possesses an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle`
      AND `the person possesses it for the purpose of committing a motor vehicle theft offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who possesses an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle for the purpose of committing a motor vehicle theft offence"

-- src:6611 | Distribution of device linked to theft
-- src:6612 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, makes, repairs, sells, offers for sale, imports into Canada, exports from Canada, distributes or makes available an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle, knowing that the device has been used or is intended to be used to commit a motor vehicle theft offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.2(2) (src:6611-6612)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes, repairs, sells, offers for sale, imports into Canada, exports from Canada, distributes or makes available the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the device has been used or is intended to be used to commit a motor vehicle theft offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.2(2) the person commits the offence of distributing a device linked to motor vehicle theft` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `the person makes, repairs, sells, offers for sale, imports into Canada, exports from Canada, distributes or makes available the thing`
      AND `the thing is an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle`
      AND `the person knows that the device has been used or is intended to be used to commit a motor vehicle theft offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, makes, repairs, sells, offers for sale, imports into Canada, exports from Canada, distributes or makes available an electronic device suitable for committing theft of a motor vehicle, knowing that the device has been used or is intended to be used to commit a motor vehicle theft offence"

-- src:6613 | Punishment
-- src:6614 | (3) Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)
-- src:6615 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years; or
-- src:6616 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.2(3) (src:6613-6616)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 333.2(3) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6617 | Forfeiture
-- src:6618 | (4) If a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1) or (2), in addition to any punishment that is imposed, the electronic device in relation to which the offence was committed may be ordered forfeited to His Majesty and may be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 333.2(4) (src:6617-6618)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 333.2(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic device is the one in relation to which the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.2(4) the electronic device may be ordered forfeited to His Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under subsection 333.2(1) or (2)` AND `the electronic device is the one in relation to which the offence was committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may be ordered forfeited") named for a conviction under (1) or (2) and the device connected with the offence

-- src:6619 | Limitation
-- src:6620 | (5) No order of forfeiture may be made under subsection (4) in respect of any thing that is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection (1) or (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 333.2(5) (src:6619-6620)
GIVEN `the thing is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection 333.2(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 333.2(5) an order of forfeiture is barred` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection 333.2(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No order of forfeiture may be made under subsection (4) in respect of any thing that is the property of a person who was not a party to the offence under subsection (1) or (2)" (a bar whose gate is unmet: reading (a) of the Marginal readings)

§§ `Section 334 -- punishment for theft`

-- "Except where otherwise provided by law": whether another provision provides the punishment (ss 333.1 and 338(2) in this Part, or a law outside this range) is an input, never guessed (fork F-334).
-- src:6621 | Punishment for theft
-- src:6622 | 334 Except where otherwise provided by law, every one who commits theft
-- src:6623 | (a) if the property stolen is a testamentary instrument or the value of what is stolen is more than $5,000, is guilty of
-- src:6624 | (i) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, or
-- src:6625 | (ii) an offence punishable on summary conviction; or
-- src:6626 | (b) if the value of what is stolen is not more than $5,000, is guilty
-- src:6627 | (i) of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or
-- src:6628 | (ii) of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 334 (src:6621-6628)
GIVEN `the property stolen is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the value of what is stolen, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `another provision of law otherwise provides the punishment for the theft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 334 the punishment for the person who commits theft` MEANS
    IF `another provision of law otherwise provides the punishment for the theft`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except where otherwise provided by law"
    ELSE CONSIDER `ccc12 or` `the property stolen is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` (JUST (`the value of what is stolen, in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000))
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a)(i) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
                                       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- (a)(ii)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)   -- (b)(i) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years
                                        , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- (b)(ii)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 2 "testamentary instrument" answer was not given and the value is not more than $5,000

§§ `Section 334.1 -- aggravating circumstances`

-- (1): the list "section 322, 343, 348, 351 or 354" is tested by section number (PLAN.md seam rule R1). An offence not in the list is NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).
-- src:6629 | Aggravating circumstance — stolen property
-- src:6630 | 334.1 (1) Without limiting the generality of section 718.2, when a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 322, 343, 348, 351 or 354, it shall consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the offence was committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant.
@ref Criminal Code s 334.1(1) (src:6629-6630)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence was committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334.1(1) the court shall consider as an aggravating circumstance that the offence was committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant` MEANS
    IF `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 322 OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 343 OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 348 OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 351 OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 354
    THEN IF `the offence was committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the offence was committed with intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant" (the fact is absent: fork F-DUTY)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence referred to in section 322, 343, 348, 351 or 354"; any other offence is outside the list, which the text does not close with "only"

-- src:6631 | Aggravating circumstance — essential infrastructure
-- src:6632 | (2) Without limiting the generality of section 718.2, when a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 322, 343 or 430, it shall consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the offence interfered with the access to or functioning of an essential infrastructure, as defined in subsection 52.1(2), or caused it to be unsafe or unfit for use.
@ref Criminal Code s 334.1(2) (src:6631-6632)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the thing is an essential infrastructure, by s 52.1(2) essential infrastructure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence interfered with the access to or functioning of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence caused it to be unsafe or unfit for use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 334.1(2) the court shall consider as an aggravating circumstance that the offence interfered with the access to or functioning of an essential infrastructure or caused it to be unsafe or unfit for use` MEANS
    IF `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 322 OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 343 OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 430
    THEN `ccc12 and` `the thing is an essential infrastructure, by s 52.1(2) essential infrastructure`
                     (JUST (`the offence interfered with the access to or functioning of it` OR `the offence caused it to be unsafe or unfit for use`))
         -- JUST FALSE: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the offence interfered with the access to or functioning of an essential infrastructure, as defined in subsection 52.1(2), or caused it to be unsafe or unfit for use" (the fact is absent: fork F-DUTY)
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 52.1(2) "essential infrastructure" answer was not given
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence referred to in section 322, 343 or 430"; any other offence is outside the list
